  "proposed_label": {
    "kind": "bug",
    "status": "agent-proposed; pending human adjudication",
    "rationale": "Replacing includes(id) with includes(pkgName) prevents an explicit package subpath from matching ssr.external. The package-level noExternal filter can then bundle that entry despite its explicit external declaration, splitting its module state from the Node-loaded copy. The fix prioritizes an exact id match and adds a state-sharing regression fixture."
  },
  "trigger": "Set ssr.external to ['external-entry/entry'] and ssr.noExternal to ['external-entry']; import the same stateful entry both directly and from another external package.",
  "fix_explanation": "Check ssr.external.includes(id) first so a specific entry is forced external; handle package-wide declarations separately and retain the externalizability check.",
  "fix_test": {
    "description": "playground/ssr-deps/__tests__/ssr-deps.spec.ts: msg from external using external entry",
    "included": true,
    "locally_run": false,
    "source_url": "https://github.com/vitejs/vite/blob/d420f01d48c2291e82410b4649f274f8d1493a27/playground/ssr-deps/__tests__/ssr-deps.spec.ts"
  },
  "caveats": [
    "The proposed finding is the loss of exact subpath matching. The same fix also adjusts package-wide externalization so non-externalizable assets still pass through checks.",
